From: wangjontao <54728149+wangjontao@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 03:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: mt7530: ignore unmapped PHY nested IRQs

On GIELINK G33Pro with MT7531, Linux 6.6.151 can receive a PHY
interrupt status bit for which no Linux IRQ mapping exists. In that
case irq_find_mapping() returns 0 and handle_nested_irq(0) dereferences
a NULL irq_desc, causing a fatal data abort at address 0xac.

Only dispatch mapped nested IRQs. The switch status bit has already
been acknowledged, so an unmapped/spurious bit can safely be skipped
while preserving normal interrupt handling for mapped PHY ports.

--- a/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530.c
@@ -1855,8 +1855,9 @@ mt7530_irq_thread_fn(int irq, void *dev_id)
 		if (BIT(p) & val) {
 			unsigned int irq;
 
 			irq = irq_find_mapping(priv->irq_domain, p);
-			handle_nested_irq(irq);
+			if (irq)
+				handle_nested_irq(irq);
 			handled = true;
 		}
 	}
